# Vercel environment variables — key-only reference. No secrets live in git.
#
# Workflow:
#   1. Fill values into deploy/vercel.production.env and deploy/vercel.preview.env
#      (both gitignored — safe to hold real secrets locally).
#   2. Vercel → groundwork → Settings → Environment Variables → paste the file's
#      contents into the key field (Vercel expands KEY=value lines into rows),
#      scoped to the matching environment. Comment lines are ignored.
#
# Named deploy/*.env, NOT .env.production / .env.preview: Next.js auto-loads
# those at build time, which would point a local prod build (and the e2e suite)
# at Neon the moment values were filled in.
#
# ── Production (most keys already set in Vercel 2026-07-29; do NOT re-paste
#    keys that exist — pasting an empty value overwrites the stored one) ──────
# DATABASE_URL           ← Neon `production` branch, pooled connection string
# BETTER_AUTH_URL        ← https://groundwork-zeta-wheat.vercel.app (stable URL)
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET     (already set)
# ADMIN_PASSWORD         (already set — the seed password for the four accounts)
# MCP_TOKEN              (already set)
# CONTENT_SOURCE         (already set)
#
# ── Preview (empty as of 2026-08-08 — needs the full set) ────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL           ← Neon `preview` branch, pooled connection string
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET     ← generate fresh; do not reuse production's
# ADMIN_PASSWORD         ← may differ from production's on purpose
# MCP_TOKEN              ← may differ from production's on purpose
# CONTENT_SOURCE         ← same value as production
# (BETTER_AUTH_URL stays unset: preview URLs differ per deploy; better-auth
#  infers the base URL from the request.)
#
# ── Later, for D1 (point the deployed instance at real repos) ────────────────
# CONTENT_SOURCE=github
# GITHUB_REPOS           ← vinhnhq/groundwork,vinhnhq/infinite-oneness
# GITHUB_TOKEN           ← fine-grained, contents:read ONLY (ADR-0010)
# GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET  ← optional, for the push webhook
#
# After setting DATABASE_URL, each Neon branch needs one-time setup from your
# machine (the seeder refuses the dev password in production — ADR-0008):
#   DATABASE_URL=<branch url> bun run migrate
#   DATABASE_URL=<branch url> ADMIN_PASSWORD=<value> bun run seed
